# IYDT-GSRP seismic analyses

These decks infer SUGAR log-yield and HOB from two seismic response channels.
Both use the shared IYDT data and application code configured in `../README`.

## Native prerequisite

The seismic coefficient priors are under the application `Phenomenology`
directory. From this directory create:

```text
ln -s ../../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp/Phenomenology Code
```

## Analyses

| Directory | Type | Decks |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `I-SUGAR-hob-0` | two-stage rapid assessment | `runMPEM.r`, `runMPEM_0.r` |
| `I-SUGAR-hob` | complete joint assessment | `runMPEM.r` |

For the rapid case:

```text
cd I-SUGAR-hob-0
R CMD BATCH runMPEM.r runMPEM.out &
```

After the background calibration finishes successfully, preserve its workspace
before starting the event calculation:

```text
cp .RData .RData-calibration
R CMD BATCH runMPEM_0.r runMPEM_0.out &
```

`runMPEM.r` writes `opt.RData`; retain it when preparing `2-Phen-sa` or
`4-Phen` starting values. Retain `.RData-calibration` as the pristine
benchmark/calibration result for all future event analyses; never replace it
with the event-modified `.RData`.

For the complete case:

```text
cd I-SUGAR-hob
R CMD BATCH runMPEM.r runMPEM.out &
```

From `Runfiles-Docker`, the corresponding analysis names are
`IYDT-gsrp/Seismic/I-SUGAR-hob-0` and
`IYDT-gsrp/Seismic/I-SUGAR-hob`. Docker supplies the local prior code inside
the snapshot and protects rapid calibration with a pristine checkpoint.

Review `iBayes`, sampler/sample settings, worker counts, and seeds in each deck
before a production run. A successful batch log ends with `proc.time()`.
